Substance, such as an antibody, created from the proteins or genes of two different species.""")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10511))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10511 "chondrification")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10511 "Formation of cartilage; transformation into cartilage.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10512))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10512 "chondroblast")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10512 "Cartilage-producing mesenchymal progenitor cell, capable of proliferating and maturing into a chondrocyte or osteoblast.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10513))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10513 "chondrocyte")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10513 "Any one of the cells embedded in the lacunae of the cartilage matrix.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10514))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10514 "chordin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10514 "Secreted protein that dorsalizes early vertebrate embryonic tissues by binding to ventralizing transforming growth factor \\(\\upbeta\\) (TGF-\\(\\upbeta\\))-like bone morphogenetic proteins, sequestering them in latent complexes.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10515))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10515 "chorioallantoic placenta")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10515 "Placenta developed from the allantois and chorion, establishing a nutritive and excretory connection between the blood of the fetus and that of the mother.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10516))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10516 "chorion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10516 """In human embryology, the cellular, outermost extra-embryonicmembrane, composed of trophoblast lined with mesoderm.
Note: The chorion develops villi, becomes vascularized by allantoic vessels, and forms the fetal part of the placenta.

In mammalian embryology, the cellular, outer extra embryonic membrane, not necessarily developing villi.
In biology, the noncellular membrane covering eggs of various animals, e.g., fish and insects.""")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10517))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10517 "chorionic gonadotropin")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10517 "Hormone secreted by the chorionic villi of the placenta in mammals, especially human chorionic gonadotropin.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10518))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10518 "chorionic sac")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10518 "Outermost membranous sac that encloses the embryo in higher vertebrates (reptiles, birds, and mammals), lined by chorion.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10519))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10519 "chorionic villus")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10519 "Any of the tiny extensions from the chorion that contain fetal blood vessels and combine with the uterine tissue to form the placenta.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10520))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10520 "chorioretinitis")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10520 "Inflammation of the choroid layer behind the retina of the eye.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10521))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10521 "choroid plexus")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10521 "Infoldings of blood vessels of the pia mater, projecting into the cerebral ventricles, covered with ependymal cells, and secreting cerebrospinal fluid.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10522))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10522 "chromaffin cell")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10522 "Cell of the adrenal medulla that secretes epinephrine and norepinephrine, and contains granules that are readily stained with chromate salts.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10523))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10523 "chromatid")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10523 "One of a pair of chromosomes arising by duplication during mitosis or by pairing during meiosis, and joined together at the centromere.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10524))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10524 "chromosomal abnormality")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10524 "Abnormality in the number or structure of chromosomes.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10525))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10525 "chromosome deletion")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10525 "Loss of a chromosome or part of a chromosome.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10526))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10526 "chromosome ring")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10526 "Abnormal chromosome in which both ends have been lost and the two broken ends have reunited to form a ring-shaped structure.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10527))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10527 "clastogen")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10527 "Agent causing chromosome breakage and (or) the consequent gain, loss, or rearrangement of pieces of chromosomes.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10528))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10528 "cleavage")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10528 "First few divisions of a fertilized egg.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10529))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10529 "meroblastic cleavage")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10529 "Partial cleavage of the egg, occurring in some animals, such as reptiles and birds, whose eggs have a large amount of yolk, resulting in unequal blastomeres and only part of the egg progressing to further cell division; the yolk mass remains and has nutritive value.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10530))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10530 "holoblastic cleavage")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10530 "Cleavage producing separate, equal blastomeres.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10531))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10531 "cleft")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10531 "Gap in soft tissue, bone, or both.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:10531 "fissure")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10532))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10532 "cleft")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10532 "Split, divided, or partly divided into two.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10533))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10533 "cleft lip")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10533 "Congenital malformation consisting of one or more clefts in the upper lip, the result of failed closure in the embryo of the maxillary and median nasal processes.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:10533 "cheiloschisis")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:10533 "hare lip")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10534))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10534 "cleft palate")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10534 "Congenital fissure along the midline of the hard palate, that may extend into the soft palate.")
AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym goldbook:10534 "palatoschisis")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10535))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10535 "cleft sternum")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10535 "Rare congenital malformation resulting from defective fusion in the embryo of paired mesodermal bands in the ventral midline.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10536))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10536 "clitoris")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10536 "Erectile body in the female genitalia, homologous with the penis in the male.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10537))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10537 "cloaca")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10537 "Common cavity at the end of the digestive tract in vertebrates (apart from most mammals) into which are released both excretory and genital products.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10538))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10538 "cloacal membrane")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:10538 "Membrane that covers the embryonic cloaca during the development of urinary and reproductive organs in those vertebrates where the cloaca occurs.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:10539))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:10539 "clover disease")
