Declaration(Class(goldbook:16203))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16203 "Franck–Condon factor")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16203 "Squared modulus of the overlap integral between the vibrational wave functions (\\(\\mathit{\\Theta}\\)) for the initial (0) and final (\\(\\rm{e}\\)) state of a given electronic transition. \\[\\left\\vert \\int \\mathit{\\Theta} _{\\rm{v'}}^{(\\rm{e})} \\mathit{\\Theta} _{\\rm{v}}^{(0)} dQ \\right\\vert^{2}\\] where the integration is over all nuclear coordinates.")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16205))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label goldbook:16205 "Lippert–Mataga equation")
AnnotationAssertion(dcterms:description goldbook:16205 """Correlation of the Stokes-shift, \\(\\Delta \\tilde{
u}\\), between the absorption and emission maxima, and the orientation polarizability \\(f(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}},n)\\) of the solvent,\\[\\Delta \\tilde{
u} = 2 \\frac{(\\boldsymbol{\\mu}_{\\rm{exc}} - \\boldsymbol{\\mu}_{\\rm{gr}})^{2}}{c h r^{3}} f(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}},n) + {\\rm{const.}}\\]with \\(\\boldsymbol{\\mu}_{\\rm{exc}}\\) and \\(\\boldsymbol{\\mu}_{\\rm{gr}}\\) the excited- and ground-state dipole moments of the dissolved molecule, respectively, \\(c\\) the speed of light, \\(h\\) the Planck constant, \\(r\\) the radius of the cavity in which the solute resides, and \\(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}}\\) the 'relative static permittivity' (formerly called dielectric constant). The expression of the Stokes shift depends only on the absolute magnitude of the difference between dipole moments and not on the angle between the dipoles. The above equation is sometimes called the Lippert equation.
The orientation polarizability is given by\\[f(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}},n) = \\frac{(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}} - 1)}{(2\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}} + 1)} - \\frac{(n^{2} - 1)}{(2n^{2} + 1)}\\]with \\(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}}\\) the relative static permittivity and \\(n\\) the refractive index of the solvent, \\(f(\\varepsilon_{\\rm{r}},n)\\) ranges from \\(\\pu{0.001}\\) in cyclohexane to \\(\\pu{0.320}\\) in water.""")
Declaration(Class(goldbook:16206))
